{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Guard the provider session: wrap run() in `with ProviderSession(...)`\n\nADR 0056 decision 2. A CORRECTNESS fix, not a refactor — independently valuable, and it should land\neven if the rest of the decomposition is descoped.\n\n## The defect (RE-MEASURED at c1fc3cee4, after e6bd and 8229 landed)\n\n    runner.py:294   provider_session = ProviderSession(cfg)   # its builders open httpx clients\n    runner.py:445   try:                                       # <-- guard starts 151 lines later\n    runner.py:495   finally:\n    runner.py:501       provider_session.close()\n\nLines 294–444 sit OUTSIDE the guard, and code in that window raises BY DESIGN:\n`_check_tool_capability(...)` is called at runner.py:337 and raises `LLMConfigError`. Anything\nraising there leaks an opened `httpx.AsyncClient` — one per affected call.\n\n`ProviderSession.__enter__` / `__exit__` ALREADY EXIST at **providers.py:323 and :326** and are\nnever used: `grep -c 'with ProviderSession' src/rebar/llm/runner.py` returns 0. Meanwhile\nproviders.py:18–24 documents \"`runner.run()` wraps its body in `with ProviderSession(cfg) as\nsession:`\" — a caller that does not exist. This ticket makes that docstring true.\n\nNOTE ON COORDINATES: an earlier version of this plan cited 301/474/582 for the three sites and\nproviders.py:295–299 for the dunders. Those were correct when written and are now ALL STALE — e6bd\nremoved the except spine and 8229 removed the settings block, shifting everything. The numbers above\nare re-measured at c1fc3cee4. **Re-locate by CONTENT, not by these offsets** if the base moves again.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove construction into a `with` covering provider resolution through the call and teardown, and drop\nthe now-redundant `finally: provider_session.close()` — `__exit__` owns it. Preserve the existing\nbest-effort semantics (close logs, never raises).\n\nCONSTRAINT: `assert_gated(\"agentic filesystem tools\")` at **runner.py:261** is a FAIL-CLOSED security\ncheck and MUST stay AHEAD of provider construction. Do not reorder it into the guarded region in a\nway that opens a client before the refusal path runs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — the `with`, and removal of the redundant `finally`.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` — **REQUIRED, and this ticket owns it.**\n  See below; omitting it breaks that test at runtime.\n- `tests/unit/` — the leak test.\n\n### THIS TICKET OWNS ONE STUB REPAIR — it is not optional and not a \"later child\" problem\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:111` defines `_NoBuildProviderSession` and\ninstalls it at :124 via `monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, \"ProviderSession\", _NoBuildProviderSession)`.\nMEASURED: that stub implements `__init__`, `supports`, `is_resolvable` and `close` — and **NOT**\n`__enter__` / `__exit__`. The moment `run()` says `with ProviderSession(cfg) as ...`, the stub stops\nsatisfying the context-manager protocol and that test fails at runtime.\n\n**Add `__enter__` (returning `self`) and `__exit__` (calling `self.close()`) to that stub IN THE SAME\nCOMMIT as the `with`.** This is a stub gaining the protocol the real object already has\n(providers.py:323/326) — NOT a weakened assertion, so it is compatible with the \"no test ASSERTION\nchanged\" criterion.\n\nThis is a DIFFERENT failure mode from the six `monkeypatch.setattr` rebind hazards the parent story\ndocuments: nothing moved modules here, so re-importing a name fixes nothing. The stub's INTERFACE\nfell behind the call site. Do not go looking for a module-globals explanation.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier with a stubbed builder recording opens/closes; no network.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts that when the pre-call window raises (e.g. `_check_tool_capability`), the\n      session's client is STILL closed — this test FAILS against today's code, so it cannot pass\n      vacuously\n- [ ] a test asserts the happy path closes EXACTLY once (a `with` plus a leftover `finally` would\n      double-close, which the stub must be able to detect)\n- [ ] `grep -c 'with ProviderSession' src/rebar/llm/runner.py` is 1, so providers.py:18–24 no longer\n      documents an absent caller\n- [ ] a close that raises is still logged and never propagated (best-effort semantics unchanged)\n- [ ] `_NoBuildProviderSession` in `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` gains\n      `__enter__`/`__exit__` in THIS commit, and that test file passes\n- [ ] `assert_gated(\"agentic filesystem tools\")` still executes BEFORE any provider client is\n      constructed — asserted by a test in which the gate refuses and NO client is opened, so the\n      fail-closed ordering is proven rather than assumed\n- [ ] the full suite passes with no test ASSERTION weakened, skipped or deleted"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785532989489166001,"uuid":"31606532-551a-450b-882e-afcce3a58759"}